      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nClarify the comments in `Platform._align_hybrid_block_size()` so they describe\r\nthe actual `mamba_cache_mode` branches.\r\n\r\nThe existing comments describe the `\"all\"` branch as using prefix caching and\r\nthe `else` branch as not using prefix caching. This is misleading because\r\n`mamba_cache_mode=\"align\"` also operates with prefix caching enabled.\r\n\r\nThe updated comments distinguish:\r\n\r\n- `\"all\"` mode\r\n- `\"none\"` and `\"align\"` modes\r\n\r\nThis is a comment-only change and does not modify runtime behavior.\r\n\r\nCloses #52895.\r\n\r\n## Duplicate-work check\r\n\r\nI searched existing issues and open PRs for the affected comments and Mamba\r\ncache-mode terminology. I did not find an existing PR that updates these\r\ncomments.\r\n\r\nRelated PR #46778 documents Mamba/hybrid prefix caching more broadly, but it\r\ndoes not modify the comments in `vllm/platforms/interface.py`.\r\n",
